---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Work with boards and folders.

USAGE
  holst board <command> [flags]

GENERAL COMMANDS
  ls:          List boards and folders as a tree or another view
  create:      Create a board or a folder

LOOK
  show:        Show boards, or a part of one, with details
  snap:        Draw a board or a part of it as PNG or SVG
  save:        Save a board or a part of it into a new folder
  export:      Save the whole board as a board file
  import:      Create a board from a board file, or write it into one

CHANGE
  edit:        Change a board's cover or note
  rename:      Rename a board or a folder
  mv:          Move a board or a folder into a folder or /
  cp:          Copy a board
  rm:          Move a board to the trash, or delete it for good
  restore:     Bring a board or folder back from the trash

YOURS
  favorite:    Add a board to favorites
  unfavorite:  Remove a board from favorites
  touch:       Mark a board as recently opened
  leave:       Leave a board you were invited to

RIGHTS AND SHARING
  grant:       Give a user a right on a board
  revoke:      Take a user's right on a board away
  share:       Change who can open, edit and copy a board
  transfer:    Make another user the owner of a board

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws   Where a board name is looked up, or where a new board goes

ARGUMENTS
  A board can be given as its id, its link or part of its name;
  several matches are listed, never guessed. A link to a frame or an object selects
  that part where a command takes a part (show, snap, save).
  A folder is given the same way; / is the root.

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b ls -w easy
  $ holst b rm "Old draft"
